  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-08-14T01:37:21.474Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "When a photo is taken with the camera, it should be saved in the Photos App, not in the File App.\n\nCurrently it is in FileApp>VRChat beta>Pictures>[daydate], but that is not easy to see, \n\nso I would like to see it changed so that it is saved in the standard photo app of the iOS/iPadOS.\n\nScope of Impact:\n\nDevice: iPhone and iPad series\n\nOS: All iOS and iPadOS supported by VRChat beta\n\nWorkaround:\n\nThe photos will be saved in the Photos App of the iOS/iPad OS.\n\nRelated Issue:\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/ios-mobile-beta/p/photo-camera-doesnt-save-photo",
